  "content": "# Bounded LRU Cache in Python Using `collections.OrderedDict`\n\n## Overview\n\nA Least Recently Used (LRU) cache is a data structure that holds a bounded set of key-value pairs. When the cache reaches its capacity and a new item needs to be added, the least recently used item is evicted. The `collections.OrderedDict` in Python provides an efficient foundation for implementing this because it maintains insertion order and supports O(1) reordering of existing elements via `move_to_end`.\n\nThis tutorial provides a complete, production-ready LRU cache implementation, explains the underlying mechanics, discusses edge cases, presents unit tests, walks through a worked example, and analyzes complexity.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Implementation\n\n```python\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nfrom typing import Any, Hashable, Optional, TypeVar\n\nK = TypeVar(\"K\", bound=Hashable)\nV = TypeVar(\"V\")\n\n\nclass LRUCache(K, V):\n    \"\"\"\n    A bounded Least Recently Used (LRU) cache.\n\n    The cache stores up to `capacity` key-value pairs. When the cache\n    is full and a new key is inserted, the least recently used entry\n    is evicted. Accessing a key (via get or put) updates its recency.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int) -> None:\n        if capacity <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Capacity must be a positive integer.\")\n        self._capacity = capacity\n        self._store: \"OrderedDict[K, V]\" = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, key: K) -> Optional[V]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieve the value associated with `key`, updating its recency.\n\n        Returns None if the key is not present in the cache.\n        \"\"\"\n        if key not in self._store:\n            return None\n        # Move the key to the end to mark it as most recently used.\n        # This is O(1) with OrderedDict.\n        self._store.move_to_end(key)\n        return self._store[key]\n\n    def put(self, key: K, value: V) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Insert or update the value for `key`, marking it as most recently used.\n\n        If the key already exists, its value is updated and its recency\n        is refreshed. If the key does not exist and the cache is at",
